# Committed template. Copy to .env.local for local development.
# Keep this file in sync whenever a config option is added or removed.
#
# IMPORTANT - local and deployed load secrets by different mechanisms, and you
# cannot reason from one to the other:
#
#   local  (`npm run dev`)  reads .env.local  -> process.env
#   local  (`npm run preview`) also reads .dev.vars for the workerd context
#   deployed                 Worker secrets   -> process.env, per request
#
# .dev.vars does NOT give `next dev` an API key. The dev server prints
# "Using secrets defined in .dev.vars", which looks like the key loaded, and
# then every generation returns 500 missing_api_key. Put the key in .env.local.
#
# In production this is a Worker secret, never a var:
#   npx wrangler secret put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY

# Server-side only. Must never reach a client component or a NEXT_PUBLIC_ var.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Unset means Anthropic direct, which is the intended configuration.
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=

# Optional model override. Defaults to claude-opus-5 in lib/config.ts.
# Note that a gateway needs a provider-prefixed id, so this and
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL must always move together.
# GAMERATOR_MODEL=
